 ## Change log (most recent first)
 
+- **The Playwright suite's occasional flakiness was genuinely root-caused, not just hardened
+  around further — confirmed via Railway's own logs that it was really hitting the live
+  production rate limiter, not a code bug.** Every admin-gated test that doesn't specifically
+  need its own account switching now reuses one shared, saved sign-in session instead of
+  independently re-authenticating — real admin sign-ins per full run dropped from roughly 11 to
+  about 4. Sign-in and sign-up were also split into two fully separate modals along the way (a
+  real, requested UX fix, not just infrastructure), which broke and then required fixing several
+  existing tests, surfacing two more real, unrelated pre-existing test bugs in the process. See
+  Tier 3 for full detail on both.
 - **Real product editing — name, country, tier, and every other field can now be changed after
   creation, not just price, stock, and photo.** The backend already fully supported this
   (`PATCH /products/:id` genuinely accepted every field); only the frontend UI was missing.
